  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EA 15/2011  - South Sudan: Access to Basic services for Returnees, IDPs and other vulnerable populat</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project will be twofold: responding to the needs of the vulnerable population in the 2 diocese within South Sudan and capacity building of the local diocesan partners (Caritas Yei &amp; Juba). The activities will deal with the emergency needs and improving access to basic services targeting vulnerable communities and households in all areas of operations; The activities to implemented are;
&#x2022;	Emergency preparedness and response 
&#x2022;	Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Promotion
&#x2022;	Shelter and Non-Food Items
&#x2022;	Food Security ( Food aid distribution)
&#x2022;	Capacity building(CMDRR)
 
The project will put emphasis on local ownership and responsibility for the program delivery with local diocesan partners. From the previous appeal EA12/2010; it was noted that the scope of assistance has to be wider than just emergency response; the focus needs to be on implementing activities that will create a positive and lasting change in the lives of beneficiaries. 

The direct beneficiaries of the project will be the staff working in the 2 Dioceses in South Sudan (Caritas Yei and Juba) and CAFOD personnel coordinating and managing the appeal .Potentially up to 15,000 direct beneficiaries will be targeted in the 2 diocese beside in direct beneficiaries within the Communities in the targeted dioceses that will also benefit through participation in emergency preparedness, response, recovery &amp; rehabilitation activities. The project will be managed by Caritas Yei, Juba and CAFOD. CAFOD will participate in the programme steering committee alongside CRS and Caritas South Sudan, and will &#x201C;twin&#x201D; with 3 dioceses to facilitate appeal activities at diocesan and community level: Yei Juba and Tombura-Yambio.

This contribution to the overall project will target the salaries for staff implementing activities in Yei and Juba diocese activities included are WASH, NFIs and food distribution and emergency preparedness and response training with emphasis in CMDRR.</narrative>
  </description>
